not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T16:46:13-08:00","id":841003,"title":"","content":"Much like the Shan'iatu, you mean? (*c*)<br /> <br /> But we have been released by our own two fingers! And also the work of everyone who poured themselves into this book. To you all, many thanks for bringing this to us. It's every bit worth the wait, and fantastic throughout.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T20:44:40-08:00","id":841098,"title":"","content":"Okay, so I don't usually read stuff in its entirety the first day it comes out. I just finished Dreams of Avirice in its entirety. That was beautiful Malcom. You somehow managed to nail both the horror of Mummy and the hopeful potential to earn your happy ending. The last two sections actually speak to something deep and profound about the human condition. Bravo!<br /> <br /> While the timeline may not be much clearer, I do think there are enough up hints in there to clarify some stuff. And yes, everyone around the Arisen's cosmology is a total dinkus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 03-03-2016, 12:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T23:34:09-08:00","id":841160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/590081-dreams-of-avarice?p=841003#post841003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Much like the Shan'iatu, you mean? (*c*)<br /> <br /> But we have been released by our own two fingers! And also the work of everyone who poured themselves into this book. To you all, many thanks for bringing this to us. It's every bit worth the wait, and fantastic throughout.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, you've been released by the work of others.<br /> <br /> As for your first question, did you guys not notice how I was patterning my behavior?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T08:08:37-08:00","id":841296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/590081-dreams-of-avarice?p=841003#post841003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But we have been released by our own two fingers!</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the context of Mummy, now I can't help but picturing those two fingers being the ones between the index and ring finger of each hand...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T17:12:02-08:00","id":841592,"title":"","content":"Preliminary Thoughts:<br /> <br /> 1) The vast majority of Mummy's gods are dicks which given the mythology of the era, doesn't really surprise me. Hell, the sumerian ones tried to kill off humanity because they were too loud. Still it seems like the Devourer hold the majority of the cards. Wonder if she's more akin to a Lower Depths being or an Abyssal one.<br /> <br /> 2) It's nice seeing Anpu's statement considering he is the god that is still roaming around and meets the Deathless every so often. Would much like to see what's his agenda now.<br /> <br /> 3) It seems like the Shan'iatu didn't have everything work out for them as they currently sit in Duat as they expect and rely on their Arisen to make living work out for them. Oddly enough, it maybe that the Deceived, with all of their rage, have the better end of the deal. <br /> <br /> 4) I need that artwork on page 15 on my wall. <i>Now.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T11:12:36-08:00","id":843053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/590081-dreams-of-avarice?p=841592#post841592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Preliminary Thoughts:<br /> <br /> 1) The vast majority of Mummy's gods are dicks which given the mythology of the era, doesn't really surprise me. Hell, the sumerian ones tried to kill off humanity because they were too loud. Still it seems like the Devourer hold the majority of the cards. Wonder if she's more akin to a Lower Depths being or an Abyssal one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I interpreted Ammut as being the Abyss itself. Starry A'aru is the Supernal and the Scroll of Ages are the power symbols which compose it. Khepera is the Fallen World and the Judges are the manifestation of the symbols of oppression Mages call the Exarchs.<br /> <br /> This is probably a flawed comparison, but it did seem to me that it meant that normal, non-Mage, humans could ascend to the Supernal if they are able to make the choice to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T07:55:53-08:00","id":843436,"title":"","content":"My interpretation was that what was described was the Truth of the phenomenal world: Ammut is oblivion, not abyssal (though would be classified as Lower Depths - only because that means &quot;I don't know, but its hungry&quot;) and a little further past Entropy; she's where ghosts go when destroyed, the bottom of the underworld, and the eventual nothingness that will consume everything, but born of this realm.<br /> <br /> Likewise it seemed to me that the Scroll of Ages was the Truth of the world; the supernal is merely the symbols that compose everything. If the supernal is the math that describes the universe, the Scroll of Ages would be the laws of physics . They do directly create one another, but one is potential, one is fact.<br /> <br /> In that sense, I could see Khepera as the supernal: the substance from which all is made, &quot;the state of existing... and am everything created, but I am not the act of creation&quot;. Atum, then, is the soul and experience ; perhaps the very force of Change which allows creation to become (or, one might say, the Principle which composes existence from its constituent parts).<br /> <b>Edit:</b> Then again, the Heretic's testimony explains that the Law of Suffering causes change, so that might have a more direct link to the Principle (at least from my understanding of it from forum conversations). However, that clashes a little with the transhumanist element the Principle inspires toward, which is why I'm interpreting it as associated with Atum. Or perhaps it could be a fragment of the time before (the law of change prior to the Exachs' influence making that suffering) which was able to hold onto its will and existence and carve out a continuing role for itself...<br /> <br /> But I could definitely see the link between the Judges and the Exarchs. As you said in my thread, the Judges and their Law of Suffering could be the causality mechanism of Fate; after the Exarchs became the symbols of oppression for all existence, the Judges would have certainly incorporated them- a blending of &quot;survival of the fittest&quot; with tyrnnical oppression (and since supernal changes are retroactive, the Judges would have always had that nature).<br /> <br /> That's just where my musings have taken me to, though","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 03-07-2016, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T09:32:37-08:00","id":843483,"title":"","content":"I think that besides being tyrants lording over humanity, the Exarchs also have as a part of their symbolism their iconic actions before and during their Ascension. Every Ascended being probably has it like that. So, in a sense the Judges are the Phenomenal manifestations of those actions, their own actions mirroring those that were already made Supernal by the Exarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T14:22:16-08:00","id":843620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/590081-dreams-of-avarice?p=843053#post843053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I interpreted Ammut as being the Abyss itself. Starry A'aru is the Supernal and the Scroll of Ages are the power symbols which compose it. Khepera is the Fallen World and the Judges are the manifestation of the symbols of oppression Mages call the Exarchs.<br /> <br /> This is probably a flawed comparison, but it did seem to me that it meant that normal, non-Mage, humans could ascend to the Supernal if they are able to make the choice to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always figured that A'aru to be the Empyrean rather than the Supernal.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T14:46:10-08:00","id":843626,"title":"","content":"How the fuck did this become a Mage thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T15:58:24-08:00","id":843653,"title":"","content":"I kind of interpreted it that Ammut is going to eat the Supernal and the Exarchs, rending all the power-playing and tyranny for naught as a massive all-hungering force bares down on not just reality but the thing that dictates its form, with A'aru being beyond reality and, therefore, beyond manipulation and mages.<br /> Otherwise you're telling me that Mages &gt; Mummy in a Mummy game, and I prefer Mummies &gt; Mages in said game.<br /> I prefer Mummies &gt; Mages period, actually, but I haven't posted about that in the Mage forums because I thought it would be kind of rude to say &quot;so the Exarchs are just pale images of the Judges which Mages only vaguely grasp and can see as little more than blurry forms through foggy water-streaked glass at a mile away, and all of the above will be devoured alongside everything else when Ammut gets her way&quot; in said forums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T16:55:47-08:00","id":843683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/590081-dreams-of-avarice?p=843626#post843626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How the fuck did this become a Mage thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Arcane....<br /> <br /> Friendship is Magic!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T17:04:14-08:00","id":843689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/590081-dreams-of-avarice?p=843653#post843653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prefer Mummies &gt; Mages period, actually, but I haven't posted about that in the Mage forums because I thought it would be kind of rude to say &quot;so the Exarchs are just pale images of the Judges which Mages only vaguely grasp and can see as little more than blurry forms through foggy water-streaked glass at a mile away, and all of the above will be devoured alongside everything else when Ammut gets her way&quot; in said forums.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rude and kind of blatantly inaccurate, to be frank, because the eternal Tyranny of human insignificance and the dictators of Suffering don't really have much in common aside from the vague sense of being alien authoritarian beings whose agendas include attempting to keep a fundamental force of entropy at bay while sequestered away in the depths of their respective cosmologies, which\u2026 describes or can conceivably describe a lot of other beings in the setting.<br /> <br /> The Judges definitely exist and could be interacted with in a muted fashion as long as one doesn't look them full in the face. Nobody's even <i>seen</i> the Exarchs directly aside from their Ministers, and those meetings blast more of their sanity and individuality away with each occasion.<br /> <br /> The Judges' connection to the Arisen is through their Will-twisted children the Shan'iatu and their means of exerting control over the Deathless is strictly carrot-and-stick. The Exarchs <i>turn their servants into extensions of themselves and in doing so burn them out</i>.<br /> <br /> The forty-two Judges cause pain with their gaze, exist in disregard of the minutia of physical scale, and created their servants with contradictory directives to appease the Devourer but are otherwise responsible for the creation of Sekhem as a natural facet of life. The numberless Exarchs are terrible to look upon as a function of their being Supernal beings who occasionally manifest avatars on Earth, charge their servants with the division of humanity and the subversion of Awakenings and Old Gods and the regulation of the Abyss to serve their Lie, and <i>are near-universally associated with symbolism of vast disharmony with their surroundings</i>.<br /> <br /> The point of the Supernal is that it describes the world, but subtranscendent perspectives of that part of the cosmology have no means of confirming whether it's a record that logs its changes or if consigning an empire to the forgotten depths of mortal memory means it's always-always only ever been an old story. There's vague similarities, but that's pretty clearly not the True Akashic Record that the Scroll of Ages is implied to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T19:08:58-08:00","id":843736,"title":"","content":"Yes, I am aware, just as A'aru does not cleanly map to the Supernal. I was being a jackass and I apologize.<br /> Here let me try again:<br /> <br /> Malcom, this book was beautiful. I've been waiting for it for months and it lived up to every expectation I had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T23:44:39-08:00","id":843834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/590081-dreams-of-avarice?p=843626#post843626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How the fuck did this become a Mage thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>The same way all Exalted threads become about Lunars, because something in the line leaves fan unfulfilled and so they hunt around others splats looking for the missing piece that will finally make their own click the rest of the way. For Mage I feel like it is the desire for all those mysteries they get their noses in should mean something. So the revelation of the supernal cosmology should matter in some broader way then just being their founding myth. <br /> <br /> Back to the Heretic: How metaphorical do you think the number of rungs in the ladder of Sutek is? On the one hand that is way more descents than I was expecting and means mummies are active something like one year in ten which is not bad all things considered. On the other, that's a lot of required descents before you are ready for apotheosis.<br /> <br /> Also, in regards to the last judge, what exactly are those secrets? While a few of the highest tier of utterance have crazy philosophical implications, none of them seem on the level of breaking the limbs of Nuit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 03-08-2016, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T00:17:37-08:00","id":843847,"title":"","content":"I thought the number of lives he lived before Apotheosis was one of the coolest parts of the book; in particular, since he <i>did</i> mention sliding back more than once, it made it think that the prospective PCs could have been <i>on</i> the path for entire lifetimes, and just forgot - the campaign would be about remembering those lives and overcoming.<br /> Mummy is always about remembering, but that really added perspective for me - every memory is leading towards <i>this.</i><br /> <br /> Also, Apotheosis is personal; I didn't read the Heretics number of lives as &quot;the minimum&quot; but as indication that &quot;it takes more than a few Descents.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T01:22:23-08:00","id":843855,"title":"","content":"Now that I've had time to look at the book, one of the things I find most interesting about it is its composite nature. Maybe it's just the academic in me, but I think we can read some interesting things into the different &quot;narrators&quot; present in the text. For instance, since <i>The Creation </i>is an ancient Iremite text rather than a (supposedly) divine revelation like <i>The Whispers of Azar</i> or <i>The Ladder of Sutek</i>, it was likely written by the Shan'iatu and probably reflects the Judges' own claims regarding their origin.<br /> <br /> Considering that Duat is a realm separate from the Underworld, and ghosts only seem to encounter the Judges if they're deliberately sent there, it seems likely that the Judges aren't as fundamental to the nature of life and the world as they would like to claim. Indeed, for beings who claim to be responsible for the creation of all living things, they seem to be pretty impotent without living (or Deathless) agents to serve them in the material world. Maybe one of the &quot;secrets&quot;of the Judges&quot; hidden in A'aru is that they're not a necessary part of the cosmos at all, and that with the vanishing of the Shan'iatu, they have no power at all except the punishments they can force on the Deathless.<br /> <br /> Of course, that would beg the question of why the Heretic would include <i>The Creation</i> in his work at all, if he knows that it's basically false.<br /> <br /> Edit: It just now occurred to me that the Heretic's title, which the translator tells us more literally means &quot;He Who Rises Above the Gods,&quot; has in interesting parallel in <i>The Creation</i>, which describes the Judges and Sutek as &quot;gods above gods.&quot; Could be a bit of foreshadowing that of the fact that the Heretic's apotheosis involves him taking on the identity of Sutek... but I kind of like the idea that the Judges themselves are heretics, creating a twisted theology in which they arrogantly place themselves above all other gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 03-08-2016, 04:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T03:29:15-08:00","id":843879,"title":"","content":"I love Mage. I really love Mage. In fact, it was the first ChroD setting that I absolutely loved after coming over as a WoD vet expecting to dive right into Vampire. But I absolutely love that CAS, when coming up with his ideas for Mummy saw a metaphysical niche that Mage left open and ran with it. I like that the universe it has is eldritch all the way down. Part of it being mysteries stacked on mysteries is one of the reasons why I like Mage and why Mage's themes of plumbing mysteries works so well for me. And it means I am beyond happy to not turn everything in the setting back towards the Supernal and Mage terminology. I understand why people do it and for the metaphysics of other lines but I think conceptions built on ideas of metaphysics X can beat metaphysics Y misses the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T07:59:08-08:00","id":843965,"title":"","content":"I didn't think of Mage at all. I *never* design with the assumption that some other game's bullshit takes precedence over what happens in this game. You can make up what you like but I, who wrote this book with a almost completely free hand, was detailing Mummy stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T10:42:32-08:00","id":844041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/590081-dreams-of-avarice?p=843855#post843855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that I've had time to look at the book, one of the things I find most interesting about it is its composite nature. Maybe it's just the academic in me, but I think we can read some interesting things into the different &quot;narrators&quot; present in the text. For instance, since <i>The Creation </i>is an ancient Iremite text rather than a (supposedly) divine revelation like <i>The Whispers of Azar</i> or <i>The Ladder of Sutek</i>, it was likely written by the Shan'iatu and probably reflects the Judges' own claims regarding their origin.<br /> <br /> Considering that Duat is a realm separate from the Underworld, and ghosts only seem to encounter the Judges if they're deliberately sent there, it seems likely that the Judges aren't as fundamental to the nature of life and the world as they would like to claim. Indeed, for beings who claim to be responsible for the creation of all living things, they seem to be pretty impotent without living (or Deathless) agents to serve them in the material world. Maybe one of the &quot;secrets&quot;of the Judges&quot; hidden in A'aru is that they're not a necessary part of the cosmos at all, and that with the vanishing of the Shan'iatu, they have no power at all except the punishments they can force on the Deathless.<br /> <br /> Of course, that would beg the question of why the Heretic would include <i>The Creation</i> in his work at all, if he knows that it's basically false.<br /> <br /> Edit: It just now occurred to me that the Heretic's title, which the translator tells us more literally means &quot;He Who Rises Above the Gods,&quot; has in interesting parallel in <i>The Creation</i>, which describes the Judges and Sutek as &quot;gods above gods.&quot; Could be a bit of foreshadowing that of the fact that the Heretic's apotheosis involves him taking on the identity of Sutek... but I kind of like the idea that the Judges themselves are heretics, creating a twisted theology in which they arrogantly place themselves above all other gods.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is somewhat borne out in the last stages of Apotheosis where they really try to stop the Arisen from continuing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T15:54:09-08:00","id":844182,"title":"","content":"On my most recent download of the PDF, my page 43 still has the bottom portion blacked out, when theyre describing Unas's reign. Is it intentional?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T16:24:21-08:00","id":844197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/590081-dreams-of-avarice?p=844182#post844182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On my most recent download of the PDF, my page 43 still has the bottom portion blacked out, when theyre describing Unas's reign. Is it intentional?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure it is. I tried copying the text there and there was nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T17:03:08-08:00","id":844215,"title":"","content":"It was mentioned in the error catching thread and called out as intentional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T21:13:34-08:00","id":845936,"title":"","content":"So I was just rereading Decieved and was intrigued by the way that the account of helping the Heretic at the end of Chapter interacts with the Heretic's own memories. Are they describing the same event? Did the Heretic seek out the Lost Guild after that first encounter? Was &quot;helping&quot; the Heretic an Obi-Won Kenobi statement meaning that the attempt to force the Heretic to reveal his True Name is what set him climbing the Ladder of Sutek? <br /> <br /> If that's the case, why did the Heretic give him the steel stylus? Pity? Mercy? Fate? Payback? Or a manipulation? <br /> <br /> It's all very interesting. What are your thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T22:34:41-08:00","id":845963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/590081-dreams-of-avarice?p=845936#post845936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I was just rereading Decieved and was intrigued by the way that the account of helping the Heretic at the end of Chapter interacts with the Heretic's own memories. Are they describing the same event? Did the Heretic seek out the Lost Guild after that first encounter? Was &amp;quot;helping&amp;quot; the Heretic an Obi-Won Kenobi statement meaning that the attempt to force the Heretic to reveal his True Name is what set him climbing the Ladder of Sutek? <br /> <br /> If that's the case, why did the Heretic give him the steel stylus? Pity? Mercy? Fate? Payback? Or a manipulation? <br /> <br /> It's all very interesting. What are your thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mercy, honestly. The Heretic wants to see all mummies escape their shackles, even the cruel, hated Deceived.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T01:44:00-08:00","id":845993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/590081-dreams-of-avarice?p=845936#post845936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I was just rereading Decieved and was intrigued by the way that the account of helping the Heretic at the end of Chapter interacts with the Heretic's own memories. Are they describing the same event? Did the Heretic seek out the Lost Guild after that first encounter? Was &quot;helping&quot; the Heretic an Obi-Won Kenobi statement meaning that the attempt to force the Heretic to reveal his True Name is what set him climbing the Ladder of Sutek?<br /> <br /> If that's the case, why did the Heretic give him the steel stylus? Pity? Mercy? Fate? Payback? Or a manipulation?<br /> <br /> It's all very interesting. What are your thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>A mix of Fate and a desire to unveil the truths of the nature of the condition that both the Arisen and Decieved share. I personally think that the stylus allowed the Temakh shard to see just how badly they screwed the pooch and give it an odd moment of self reflection on an otherwise quite self obsessed entity. It is an item that reveals the nature of things. A mirror that one you can't look away from and your reflection shows that you can do better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T05:56:33-08:00","id":846039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/590081-dreams-of-avarice?p=843847#post843847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the number of lives he lived before Apotheosis was one of the coolest parts of the book; in particular, since he <i>did</i> mention sliding back more than once, it made it think that the prospective PCs could have been <i>on</i> the path for entire lifetimes, and just forgot - the campaign would be about remembering those lives and overcoming.<br /> Mummy is always about remembering, but that really added perspective for me - every memory is leading towards <i>this.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>If I was going to compare this to something from another game line, it would be Promethean's Pilgrimmage.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T16:43:56-08:00","id":846330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/590081-dreams-of-avarice?p=845963#post845963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mercy, honestly. The Heretic wants to see all mummies escape their shackles, even the cruel, hated Deceived.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree with you, although I do find it interesting that the Stylus seems to help the Temakh in addition to the Mummy. I feel like Shock may be right about allowing the Temakh to self-reflect, and perhaps free it from its own shackles, thus freeing the Mummies that it has chained. <br /> <br /> In other news, I did a bit more cross-referencing, this time with Guildhalls of the Deathless. Antu-Herap, The Prince of Glass, met the Heretic after the latter's Apotheosis, pursing Iremite texts during the Second Sothic Turn. Nefernewet is described as having met Urmontu after Constantine the Great &quot;destroyed religious variety in [Byzantium].&quot; That statement could apply at pretty much any time in Constantine's reign as Augustus or sole Emperor, however it is likely that the earliest date it could apply to was the Edict of Milan in February of 313 CE. The Heretic gives his True Name as Azar sometime between then an 337, when ends with him in Henet. He has to Arise again, then achieve Apotheosis, then encounter The Prince of Glass all before 551 CE, which is a relatively short time period of the Arisen. It doesn't mean too much, but it is interesting to see how the journey played out. The Prince of Glass may very well have been the first Mummy that the Heretic encountered after Apotheosis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T17:37:49-08:00","id":846347,"title":"","content":"I hadn't even thought to cross reference Guildhalls. I wonder if the Su-Menent chapter will seem less confusing. Speaking of cross referencing, in Book of the Deceived, the temakh mentions it told a pair of lies in the text deliberately. I think, using Dreams of Avarice, we might be able to find the contradiction, and thus, find the lies the Deceived spoke of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T17:45:43-08:00","id":846351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/590081-dreams-of-avarice?p=846347#post846347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hadn't even thought to cross reference Guildhalls. I wonder if the Su-Menent chapter will seem less confusing. Speaking of cross referencing, in Book of the Deceived, the temakh mentions it told a pair of lies in the text deliberately. I think, using Dreams of Avarice, we might be able to find the contradiction, and thus, find the lies the Deceived spoke of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, maybe not. The stylus is supposed to allow the Deceived to record its Memories, but has the limitation of blurring them with the Decieved's desires for what it wishes had actually happened. Unless, of course, that was one of the lies. <br /> <br /> Plus, I think there were way more places that the account contradicted itself and Dreams of Avarice than two. That's okay though, it would still be an interesting exercise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T18:04:33-08:00","id":846355,"title":"","content":"I honestly think the stylus is just a pen. The way it described it's curses just feels like writing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T18:07:22-08:00","id":846357,"title":"","content":"It may very well be... although given that the account has been pressed into stone, there's got to be something magic to it. Maybe all it does if give the Deceived a normal, human Memory while its being used to write?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T22:19:15-08:00","id":846449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/590081-dreams-of-avarice?p=846330#post846330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In other news, I did a bit more cross-referencing, this time with Guildhalls of the Deathless. Antu-Herap, The Prince of Glass, met the Heretic after the latter's Apotheosis, pursing Iremite texts during the Second Sothic Turn. Nefernewet is described as having met Urmontu after Constantine the Great &amp;quot;destroyed religious variety in [Byzantium].&amp;quot; That statement could apply at pretty much any time in Constantine's reign as Augustus or sole Emperor, however it is likely that the earliest date it could apply to was the Edict of Milan in February of 313 CE. The Heretic gives his True Name as Azar sometime between then an 337, when ends with him in Henet. He has to Arise again, then achieve Apotheosis, then encounter The Prince of Glass all before 551 CE, which is a relatively short time period of the Arisen. It doesn't mean too much, but it is interesting to see how the journey played out. The Prince of Glass may very well have been the first Mummy that the Heretic encountered after Apotheosis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I may have jumped the gun a little here. The Storyteller's section says that the Heretic achieved Apotheosis some time in the last century, so clearly what the Prince of Glass remembers is the Heretic as a Mummy, but one in search of the truth and his Memory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T16:42:53-07:00","id":850312,"title":"","content":"Holy. Freaking. Crap. I just finished reading Dreams of Avarice and it is glorious beyond measure. I don't think I'll look at Mummy quite the same way ever again. Heck, if the Judges are actually major players in CofD cosmology, I might never look at the CofD <i>universe </i>the same way ever again. The nature of the Law of Suffering, of Will, and what it means to be a human in the eyes of the Judges, is a terribly disheartening thing, but it's giving me so much inspiration for Mummy stuff. I'm feeling incredibly ambitious in terms of trying to put together ideas of what Irem was like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T17:37:02-07:00","id":850338,"title":"","content":"While I do agree that Dreams of Avarice is <i>awesome</i>, my own perception is that unreliable narrators are kind of a theme in mummy. It sort of goes hand-in-hand with the loss of memory thing: it's hard to catch a lie if you don't remember anything about the truth, or even what reasons you might have not to trust the lair. And in the CofD - <i>particulary</i> in Mummy - <i>everybody </i>lies. Positing that the Heretic is an exception to that rule seems a bit naive, though I may just be cynical. <br /> <br /> Although, even if we can trust the Heretic's word implicitly, he didn't actually write all of <i>Dreams of Avarice</i>. There's not really any obvious way for him to know if the Iremite scriptures he included in the book are at all true, or if they're (partly or entirely) a fiction cooked up by the Judges or the Shan'iatu. Actually, that's probably why he sought out the Deceived who wrote <i>Why the Stars Fall</i>; if anybody now active in the world can give insight into the actual history of creation before the later days of the Nameless Empire, it would be one of the shattered Temakh carried by the Deceived.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thanke